{{- /*
agy (Antigravity CLI): ~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json, the global MCP servers
(see the "MCP Servers (mcp_config.json)" doc embedded in agy; checked on 1.5.12).

tmux: the tmux MCP server (spawn_subagent, wait_subagents, list_panes,
message_agent, ...; see ~/code/tmux-mcp/README.md). Wired here for the
external-subagents feature (plan U9).

Why stdio and not the shared HTTP server on 127.0.0.1:7998:
  The HTTP server wants `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, with the token in
  ~/.local/state/tmux-mcp/token. agy supports a `url` with static `headers`
  only. Its MCP configs do NOT expand environment variables, and it has no
  token-file or headers-helper option, so the only HTTP form would inline the
  secret, which this repo never does. agy runs its own copy of the same server
  over stdio instead (`server.ts --stdio`, the transport the test suite
  uses). A local child process needs no token. Same tools; the caller's tab
  comes from TMUX_PANE when agy passes its env on, otherwise from process
  ancestry (agy -> bun).
  Cost: one bun process per agy session, idle between calls.

env: PATH and TMUX_MCP_HIDE_SESSIONS match the LaunchAgent
(com.mackhaymond.tmux-mcp), so tmux and agent-spawn resolve the same way.
No per-call timeout key is documented for agy. Keep wait_subagents calls at
the default 45 s timeout_s and call again.

Managed by chezmoi: `agy mcp add` writes here too, so add any other server
in this template, or `chezmoi apply` will drop it.
Without MCP, agy still has the CLI: `agent-spawn` and
~/.agents/skills/tmux-workspace/scripts/tmux-mcp-call.py.
*/ -}}
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "tmux": {
      "command": {{ joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir ".bun/bin/bun" | toJson }},
      "args": [
        {{ joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir "code/tmux-mcp/src/server.ts" | toJson }},
        "--stdio"
      ],
      "env": {
        "PATH": "/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin",
        "TMUX_MCP_HIDE_SESSIONS": "agents,stash,scratch,tasks",
        "LANG": "en_US.UTF-8"
      }
    }
  }
}
